When a route/direction has only `exact_times=0` frequency trips at this stop, `routeDirectionScheduleMap` has no entry for the route, so `directionMap` is a nil map and `directionMap[dirID]` yields a nil slice. `NewStopRouteDirectionSchedule` special-cases nil `frequencies` (`[]ScheduleFrequency{}`) but passes `stopTimes` straight through, so the response emits `"scheduleStopTimes": null`.

`testdata/openapi.yml` lists `scheduleStopTimes` in `StopRouteDirectionSchedule.required`, and Java OBA emits an empty list — a `null` here will break clients that iterate the array unguarded. The fixture in `frequency_fixture_test.go` puts a plain scheduled trip in the same route+direction as the frequency trips, so this path is never exercised by the new tests.

Simplest fix is to mirror the frequencies handling in `NewStopRouteDirectionSchedule`:

```suggestion
			stopTimes := directionMap[dirID]
			if stopTimes == nil {
				stopTimes = []models.ScheduleStopTime{}
			}
			directionSchedule := models.NewStopRouteDirectionSchedule(tripHeadsign, stopTimes, frequencies)
```

